## 16. Important Business Rules

1. Each stock-taking session must have a unique session number.
2. A session must be associated with a stock-taking date and warehouse.
3. Each count must identify the employee responsible.
4. Product quantities must be normalized to base inventory units.
5. Stock-count entries must support offline storage.
6. Synchronization must be idempotent.
7. Duplicate API requests must not duplicate count records.
8. Blind-count mode must not expose system quantities through API responses to counting users.
9. Submitted sessions must be protected from unauthorized changes.
10. Recount history must be preserved.
11. Approval and posting must be separate operations.
12. Stock adjustments must be generated only from approved and reconciled quantities.
13. Sessions must not be posted more than once.
14. All operations must respect company, branch, warehouse, and user permissions.
15. Incomplete offline counts must never be silently discarded.
16. All quantities must support appropriate decimal precision for the product's unit of measure.

